From ae943eac22f8809a98b3799e35966720f14dd9b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Uwe Augustin <Info@FlapsOnline.de>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 16:21:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] OpenVario: choose the firmware image in XCSoar and quit for
 the upgrade

Started from within XCSoar, fw-upgrade.sh did not get the screen on the
device: XCSoar stayed visible with the button pressed, and an Enter
started the upgrade without showing which image it would flash.

A click on the firmware row now lists the images in data/download and
on the USB stick (openvario/images), filtered to the hardware of the
device with a button to show all.  The chosen image becomes the only
entry of data/images, as a hard link into data/download; an image from
the stick is copied there first, because a hard link cannot leave the
data partition, and it stays available without the stick.  XCSoar then
saves the profile and quits with exit code 205, which the start script
of the image answers by running fw-upgrade.sh on the console with that
image.

This is the protocol of the OpenSoaring OpenVario image and not meant
for upstream; the image carries it as a patch.
